# RAHBAR .gitignore
#
# Rules (sec. 4.7, sec. 8):
# - *-secret.yaml is gitignored: Secrets are created from the command line,
#   never from a committed file. Base64 is encoding, not encryption.
# - The corpus PDFs are NOT committed: commit corpus/MANIFEST.md + the
#   fetch script instead (sec. 2). corpus/raw/ and *.pdf under corpus/
#   stay local.
# - eval/results.json MUST be COMMITTED (sec. 8: submit results.json and
#   baseline.json), so it is deliberately NOT ignored here.

# --- Secrets (never commit) ---
*-secret.yaml
**/*-secret.yaml
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*

# --- Corpus PDFs (MANIFEST.md + fetch script are committed instead) ---
corpus/raw/
corpus/datalake/
corpus/quarantine/
corpus/archive/
corpus/reports/
corpus/raw/*.pdf
corpus/raw/**/*.pdf

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.hypothesis/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# --- Agent tooling / internal logs ---
.agents/

# --- Local tooling / OS ---
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.log

# --- Local assignment / reference specs ---
assignment_03.md
ragops_operating_and_managing_retrieval_augmented_generation_pipelines.md
